BASIC:

Q1. What is Terraform, and what problem does it solve?
A1. An open-source Infrastructure as Code (IaC) tool by HashiCorp. It lets you define, provision, and manage cloud and on-prem infrastructure using declarative configuration files. It solves manual provisioning, inconsistency, and lack of version control for infrastructure.

Q2. What is Infrastructure as Code (IaC)?
A2. Managing infrastructure through code instead of manual processes. Benefits: repeatability, version control, automation, consistency, and easier collaboration.

Q3. What language does Terraform use?
A3. HCL (HashiCorp Configuration Language). JSON is also supported.

Q4. What are providers?
A4. Plugins that let Terraform talk to platform APIs such as AWS, Azure, GCP, Kubernetes, GitHub.
    provider "aws" {
      region = "us-east-1"
    }

Q5. Difference between init, plan, apply, destroy?
A5. init    -> downloads providers/modules, initializes backend
    plan    -> shows what changes will be made (dry run)
    apply   -> executes the changes
    destroy -> removes all managed infrastructure

Q6. What is a resource block? Give an example.
A6. It declares an infrastructure object to create/manage.
    resource "aws_instance" "web" {
      ami           = "ami-0abcdef123"
      instance_type = "t3.micro"
    }
    Syntax: resource "<type>" "<local_name>" { ... }

Q7. What are variables and outputs?
A7. Variables = inputs that parameterize configuration.
    Outputs   = values exposed after apply (e.g., IP address) for users or other modules.
    variable "region" { default = "us-east-1" }
    output "instance_ip" { value = aws_instance.web.public_ip }

Q8. What is the Terraform state file?
A8. terraform.tfstate is a JSON file mapping your config to real-world resources. Terraform uses it to track metadata, compute diffs, and improve performance. It can contain sensitive data, so protect it.

Q9. terraform.tfvars vs variables.tf?
A9. variables.tf   -> DECLARES variables (name, type, default, description)
    terraform.tfvars -> ASSIGNS values to those variables

Q10. What do terraform fmt and terraform validate do?
A10. fmt      -> formats code to canonical style
     validate -> checks syntax and internal consistency (no cloud calls)


